---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CategoryHub from '../../components/CategoryHub.astro';
import { relFor } from '../../lib/affiliate-value';
import AffiliateDisclosure from '../../components/AffiliateDisclosure.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Grant research software for nonprofits"
  description="The grant research tools worth paying for, compared by price and shop size: Instrumentl, GrantStation, Candid, and Grants.gov."
  section="grant-research">
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Grant research' }]} />
    <section class="prose" style="margin-top: 1.2rem;">
      <p class="kicker">Category guide</p>
      <h1>Grant research software</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Grant tools answer two questions: which funders are worth your hours, and
        how fast can you get a strong application out the door. Credible options
        run from about $199 a year to $500 a month, and the right one depends on
        your application volume.
      </p>

      <AffiliateDisclosure />
    </section>

    <CategoryHub category="grant-research" part="table" />

    <section class="prose" style="max-width: none;">


      <h2>How to choose</h2>
      <p>
        Match the tool to your volume. A handful of applications a year:
        <a href="/go/grantstation" rel={relFor('grantstation')}>GrantStation</a>
        (about $199/yr through TechSoup) plus free library access to
        <a href="/go/candid" rel={relFor('candid')}>Candid</a> covers it, and a
        general AI assistant will draft faster than any grant-specific writing
        tool you would pay for at that volume. Ten or more concurrent
        applications: <a href="/go/instrumentl" rel={relFor('instrumentl')}>Instrumentl</a>
        (from $179/mo) replaces both the searching and the tracking spreadsheet,
        and its 14-day trial is the fastest way to see whether the matching earns
        the price for your programs.
      </p>
      <p>
        One rule keeps this category honest: buy research software when finding
        funders is the bottleneck. If drafting is the bottleneck instead, the
        honest answer is that a $20/month general AI assistant handles first
        drafts as well as the grant-specific writing tools we have looked at,
        and no software fixes a program that isn't fundable yet.
      </p>
    </section>

    <CategoryHub category="grant-research" part="tools" />

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        See where grant tools fit in <a href="/stacks/under-250k/">the grassroots
        stack</a>, <a href="/stacks/250k-1m/">the $250k-$1M stack</a>, and
        <a href="/stacks/1m-5m/">the $1M-$5M stack</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
